# Generated icon library sources — written by the `generate-icons` target
# (nx run <set>:generate-icons) at build time from packages/<set>/icon-set.json.
# Covers the primary entry (src/lib/icons/) and any secondary entry points
# (src/<entry>/lib/icons/).
packages/**/icons/

# Heavy per-set icon reference JSON — written by the `update-reference` target
# (nx run <set>:update-reference) from node_modules/@iconify/json on demand.
# No set ships its JSON in git (lucide included): every set regenerates it
# locally, so a fresh clone stays light. `icon-entries.json` (the split plan)
# IS tracked: it is small and part of the package config.
packages/*/icon-set.json
packages/**/README.md

# Generated docs manifest assets — written by the `generate-docs-manifest`
# target (nx run internal-docs:generate-docs-manifest) at build time from
# packages/*/icon-set.json into apps/docs/public/icons/.
apps/docs/public/icons/

# The static lazy-import map MUST stay committed: Nx derives internal-docs'
# dependency graph from it (231 library imports). A fresh CI runner computes
# the graph before the generate-docs-manifest target runs, so an ignored map
# leaves internal-docs with zero dependencies and its build cannot chain the
# generate-icons tasks that produce src/lib/icons. Regeneration is
# deterministic, so the committed file stays in sync with the packages.

# Generated SEO / AI-discovery files — emitted by the same target into
# apps/docs/public/ (sitemap.xml, robots.txt, llms.txt, llms-full.txt).
apps/docs/public/sitemap.xml
apps/docs/public/robots.txt
apps/docs/public/llms.txt
apps/docs/public/llms-full.txt
